From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: weizxfree <weizhangxiang2022@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 05:35:34 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] fix(convert): conversion fixes for a running app that
 replaces LibreOffice

KnowWork retires LibreOffice in favour of GenOffice for conversions (previews,
legacy formats, skill exports). Each fix below was found by converting the same
real documents with both and comparing.

- doc2docx: keep the outline of a converted .doc as Heading styles. Styles were
  flattened into direct formatting, so a converted .doc kept its headings' look
  but no paragraph was a heading (a real procurement plan: 47 in, 0 out). A
  paragraph now gets Heading N from its outline level the way Word reads it (its
  own outline level, then each style down the chain, a built-in heading style
  implying its level, 9 being body text); the Heading styles carry only the
  outline level, so the document renders pixel-identical. Empty heading-styled
  paragraphs stay out of the outline, as in Word.
- sheets: export_document in a running app wrote no PDF. The hidden window the
  main process opens for the export had its output path honoured only in a
  --headless-export run, so the running app put up a save dialog instead (no one
  answers it in web-server mode). A window the main process opened for an export
  now writes where it was told and does not open the file afterwards; any other
  window still asks.
- sheets print: text that does not wrap spills into the empty cells beside it,
  as Excel prints it (left-aligned to the right, right-aligned to the left,
  centred evenly both ways, up to the first cell with content; numbers never
  do). Every cell was clipped at its own edge, so a note typed into one cell of
  a wide empty row came out cut off.
- sheets print: a picture anchored to one cell (oneCellAnchor) keeps its size as
  offsets past that cell while its end marker stays on it, and the print area
  went by the end marker, so a tall flow chart printed as a sliver on one page.
  The area now reaches as far as such a picture does; a real end marker
  (twoCellAnchor) stays authoritative.
- odf2ooxml: a shape holding text in an .odp keeps the text as a text box at the
  shape's place. LibreOffice saves a PowerPoint text box as draw:custom-shape
  and generated decks do the same, so dropping every shape converted such decks
  to slides with no text at all (3 real decks: 0 characters out, now identical
  to LibreOffice's). The shape's outline and fill are reported as dropped.
- docs: prune the pagination preview's per-page clones from about 3 pages of 10k
  elements (CLONE_PRUNE_ELEMENT_BUDGET 1M -> 30k). Each preview page carried a
  full copy of the document below that budget, so a 49-page tender put 465k
  elements in the preview and every style recalc and print-media flip walked
  all of them: its PDF export took ~80 s (110 s on Linux), now ~18 s (22 s).
  Six real documents export the same pages pixel for pixel, apart from
  sub-pixel offsets on a few pages.
